x86_64-windows  Two names cxx1 emits and clang does not: `??_DD1@@QEAAXXZ` and `??_DD2@@QEAAXXZ`, the vbase destructors of the two middle classes. That is Itanium's D1 under its Microsoft name - it destroys the class's own part and then the virtual bases - and this case never destroys a D1 or a D2 as a *complete* object, so clang emits neither. cxx1 emits one beside every destructor of a class with a virtual base, the way it emits D1 beside every D2, and an unused COMDAT definition costs a fold. **The names this case is about all agree**: `??_8D1@@7B@`, `??_8D2@@7B@`, `??_8Dia@@7BD1@@@` and `??_8Dia@@7BD2@@@`, checked against cl itself by names-vs-cl on the box. The Itanium columns agree in full since 2026-09-15, VTTs and construction vtables included.
